title: ClaudeHistory misses a same-size rewrite within the same second
updated: 2026-11-10T03:58:04Z
---

Found during k85 (already in HEAD before it). The metadata cache treats a file as unchanged when dev, inode, size and mtime match. mtime is whole seconds (stat), so a rewrite in place that keeps the size within the same second is not seen until the file changes again. Claude Code only appends, so in practice rare. Options: Time::HiRes::stat for a sub-second mtime, or also compare ctime. Decide whether it is worth it.

Decision by the main session (2026-11-10), under the maintainer's 'erledige die tickets von karr'; the maintainer may veto: yes. The freshness check compares mtime with sub-second precision (Time::HiRes::stat, core), so a same-size rewrite within a second is seen. Cheap: one stat call, no new state.

Done by mcp-hub-worker in worktree main (uncommitted); red on a clean HEAD export, green with the patch; t/native/ + t/hub.t pass under EV and Poll (22 files, 350 tests) with all six natives cards applied. Apply order k99, k111, k163, k172, k173, k179 (scratchpad w-kNNN/incr.patch each). k99: _refresh reads mtime with Time::HiRes::stat (path stat and the stat after the read), so a same-size rewrite within one second is read again.

